From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nuubOS <nuubos@localhost>
Date: Sun, 28 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm: sun4i: preserve H700 final frame during shutdown

nuubOS deliberately renders its final Restart/Power Off frame into the
kernel-owned DRM fbdev buffer before entering the kernel reboot/poweroff
path.

The generic sun4i platform-driver shutdown callback subsequently calls
drm_atomic_helper_shutdown(), disabling the active CRTC/panel and turning
the display black well before the SoC actually resets or powers off.

H700 handhelds use the display as part of the product lifecycle UX.
Preserve the already-programmed scanout state during platform-driver
shutdown on H700 only. Normal driver unbind/remove still uses the generic
DRM shutdown path.

This keeps the final framebuffer visible until reset/power removal without
changing shutdown semantics on non-H700 sun4i platforms.

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_drv.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_drv.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_drv.c
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include <linux/dma-mapping.h>
 #include <linux/kfifo.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/of_graph.h>
 #include <linux/of_reserved_mem.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
@@ -419,6 +420,15 @@ static void sun4i_drv_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)

 static void sun4i_drv_shutdown(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
+	/*
+	 * nuubOS H700 lifecycle frames are intentionally left in the
+	 * kernel-owned fbdev scanout until the machine actually resets or
+	 * loses power. drm_atomic_helper_shutdown() would blank the panel
+	 * prematurely during device_shutdown().
+	 */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("allwinner,sun50i-h700"))
+		return;
+
 	drm_atomic_helper_shutdown(platform_get_drvdata(pdev));
 }

